{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing task #5386 from a work queue in the go-unix-utils project. The task is a \"stitch\" task to implement srd054-tr requirements R3.1, R3.2, and R3.3 for the `cmd/tr` utility (character translator). Specifically:\n   - **R3.1**: `[:lower:]` to `[:upper:]` must translate lowercase to uppercase; `[:upper:]` to `[:lower:]` must translate uppercase to lowercase.\n   - **R3.2**: When translating (not deleting), SET2 must not be empty. If SET2 is omitted, must print a usage error.\n   - **R3.3**: Equivalence classes `[=CHAR=]` must be supported in SET2 for specifying characters that sort identically.\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/tr/main.go` and `cmd/tr/tr_test.go`. Acceptance criteria require the code to compile, pass differential tests against `gtr` (GNU tr), and match gtr output for R3.1-R3.3 behaviors.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against GNU reference binary (`gtr`)\n   - POSIX character classes (`[:lower:]`, `[:upper:]`, etc.) in SET specifications\n   - Equivalence classes (`[=CHAR=]`) in SET specifications\n   - Character translation table construction via positional mapping between SET1 and SET2\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - SET expansion including ranges, octal escapes, backslash escapes, repetitions, and character classes\n   - Complement mode (`-c`/`-C`), delete mode (`-d`), squeeze mode (`-s`)\n   - `LC_ALL=C` environment for tests (single-byte encoding only)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd054-tr.yaml`** (read, full SRD)\n     - Contains the full specification for tr. R3 group defines \"Character class translation pairs\":\n       - R3.1: lower↔upper class translation\n       - R3.2: SET2 must not be empty when translating\n       - R3.3: Equivalence classes [=CHAR=] support\n     - Non-goals: no multibyte support, no file arguments\n   \n   - **`cmd/tr/main.go`** (read, 452 lines, to be modified)\n     - Existing implementation covers R1.1-R1.4 and R2.1-R2.4\n     - Key functions: `parseArgs`, `validateOperands`, `run`, `expandSet`, `buildTable`, `process`, `complementSet`, `memberSet`\n     - `expandCharClass` (lines 296-330) already handles lower/upper/digit/alpha/alnum/blank/space/cntrl/print/graph/punct/xdigit classes\n     - `parseEquivClass` (lines 348-355) already parses `[=CHAR=]` and returns single byte\n     - `validateOperands` (lines 93-111) already checks for missing operands\n     - `run` function (lines 113-152) checks `len(set2) == 0` at line 143 and returns error\n     - `buildTable` (lines 176-189) maps SET1 to SET2 positionally, extending SET2's last char\n   \n   - **`cmd/tr/tr_test.go`** (read, 59 lines, to be modified)\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gtr\")`\n     - Already has 36 test cases including `class_lower_upper`, `class_upper_lower`, `class_digit_replace`\n     - Tests cover basic translation, delete, squeeze, complement, combined flags, ranges, classes, octal/escape sequences, error cases\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The task had just begun with file reads; no code was written or compiled.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Initial analysis phase only. Read the SRD and existing code to understand what R3.1-R3.3 require and what already exists.\n   - The existing code appears to already have partial implementations for all three requirements:\n     - R3.1: `expandCharClass` handles lower/upper, and `buildTable` does positional mapping - so `[:lower:]` → `[:upper:]` should already map a→A, b→B, etc.\n     - R3.2: `validateOperands` and the `len(set2) == 0` check in `run` already handle empty SET2\n     - R3.3: `parseEquivClass` already parses `[=CHAR=]` syntax\n   - Need to verify these work correctly with gtr and add targeted test cases to confirm R3.1-R3.3 specifically.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Large task description with full project context, SRD specifications, architecture, execution constitution, coding standards, and specific task requirements for implementing srd054-tr R3.1-R3.3.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement any missing functionality for R3.1 (class-to-class translation lower↔upper)\n   - Implement any missing functionality for R3.2 (SET2 empty validation when translating)\n   - Implement any missing functionality for R3.3 (equivalence classes [=CHAR=] in SET2)\n   - Add differential test cases covering R3.1, R3.2, R3.3 to `cmd/tr/tr_test.go`\n   - Run `go build ./cmd/tr/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/tr/ -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just completed reading the three required files (SRD, main.go, tr_test.go) and was about to begin the implementation phase. No code changes have been made yet. The analysis of existing code suggests that much of R3.1-R3.3 functionality may already be present from the R1/R2 implementation, but the task requires:\n   1. Verifying/completing the implementations\n   2. Adding targeted test cases specifically for R3.1-R3.3 behaviors\n   3. Ensuring all acceptance criteria pass\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   The next step is to analyze what's actually missing from the existing implementation for R3.1-R3.3, then modify `cmd/tr/main.go` if needed and add test cases to `cmd/tr/tr_test.go`. Based on the task description: \"Add functionality for srd054 requirements R3.1, R3.2, R3.3\" and \"Add differential test cases covering R3.1, R3.2, R3.3\". The key areas to verify/implement:\n   \n   - For R3.1: Verify that `[:lower:]`→`[:upper:]` and `[:upper:]`→`[:lower:]` work correctly with the positional mapping. May need to add explicit test cases.\n   - For R3.2: Verify the error message matches gtr's error message format. Add test cases for error scenarios (missing SET2 when translating).\n   - For R3.3: Verify `[=CHAR=]` works in SET2 context. Add test cases for equivalence classes.\n   - Run `go build -o bin/tr ./cmd/tr/` and `go test ./cmd/tr/ -count=1` to verify.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5386/2c6b651d-10da-4679-b0c4-38e48c4ea296.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c6b651d-10da-4679-b0c4-38e48c4ea296","uuid":"b4ed268d-7018-41d1-b581-7c4d30777f7b","timestamp":"2026-05-20T23:33:55.494Z","isSynthetic":true}
